lesson physics-year-review-5 v=1 format=review grade=5 unit=9 subject=physics levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Physics review: the fifth year"
  goal "Look back over the year: the pendulum, floating and water pressure, streamlining, the planets, mirrors and lenses, electromagnets and circuit diagrams."

  warm-up {
    show physics.swing-one-swing l=4 easy-l=3 hard-l=7
    show physics.upthrust-read a=9 u=2 easy-a=7 easy-u=1 hard-a=10 hard-u=4
    show physics.reflect-out a=50 easy-a=40 hard-a=55
  }
  exercises {
    show physics.displace-push r=300 a=8 easy-r=200 easy-a=6 hard-r=400 hard-a=10
    show physics.pressure-depth q=0 d=3.5 easy-d=2 hard-q=1 hard-d=2.5
    show physics.drop-bottom s="cube" easy-s="ball" hard-s="flat"
    show physics.scale-model-distance k=4 easy-k=7 hard-k=5
    show physics.weight-planet p=1 m=10 easy-p=2 easy-m=2 hard-m=30
    show physics.lens-focus f=14 easy-f=10 hard-f=36
    show physics.telescope-magnify fo=90 fe=5 easy-fo=60 easy-fe=2 hard-fo=60 hard-fe=4
    show physics.coil-predict t=40 c=2 easy-t=20 easy-c=1 hard-t=30 hard-c=3
    show physics.symbol-volts c=4 b=2 easy-c=4 easy-b=1 hard-c=2 hard-b=3
  }
  puzzle stars=2 {
    show physics.coil-double v=2 easy-v=1 hard-v=0
  }
  puzzle stars=3 {
    show physics.swing-length-for-time v=2 easy-v=0 hard-v=3
  }

  grown-ups """
    This is a check, not a test, to do in the old city at the end of the fifth year. The warm-up is
    the first question of three lessons: one swing from ten on a stopwatch, the water's push on a
    stone, and the angle a beam leaves a mirror at. The exercises take one question each from the
    year: the push from the water a lump pushes aside, the push at the bottom of a lock, how long a
    shape takes to sink, a planet's place in the corridor model, a weight on another world, the
    focus of a lens, how many times bigger a telescope shows the Moon, the clips an electromagnet
    holds, and the volts in a circuit diagram. Anything that needs the way in again is worth another
    week with that lesson, and everything else can move on. The two puzzles are there to be enjoyed:
    the electromagnet puzzle is answered by working out every change, and the pendulum puzzle by
    spotting that four times the string gives twice the time. Ask for the reason as well as the
    number.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the numbers are the smallest of each lesson: short strings, a push of one newton, whole-metre depths, Uranus in the corridor, Jupiter's pull on 2 kg, focuses in tens, a coil on one cell and volts from four cells, and the pendulum puzzle asks for 20 seconds."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the numbers are the largest: long strings, a push of four newtons, a depth worked back from a push, the flat shape's slow sink, Jupiter's place in tenths of a centimetre, Mars's pull on 30 kg, a focus between the marks, a coil on three cells, volts shared among three bulbs, and the pendulum puzzle asks for 28 seconds."
  }
}
